## The block: the 9 extra rows fail on a version field

The expected value says the union passes 224 rows, 0 rows pass in both, and each folder has 0
rows that fail for another reason. The run gives 215 rows, 0 rows in both, and 9 rows in folder 1
that fail for another reason.

All 9 rows fail on one rule. The rule sits in `dashboard/lib/storytime/print/picture-check.ts:188`.
The N in the file name must equal the selectedVersion of the job. The message of each row reads:

```
picture batch: the files "<row id>-v1.png" and "<row id>-line-v1.png" of the row <row id> are
version 1; the job selected version 2, so N must equal the selected version
```

The manifest of folder 1 holds 9 jobs whose selectedVersion is 2 or 3. The only candidate of each
of these jobs names a `-v1.png` file and a `-line-v1.png` file. The candidate version field and
the file names disagree.

