## The probe: the 9 rows hold good pictures

A probe in `/tmp/opencode/t27/` repaired the 9 version fields to the N in the file names. The
probe folder held hard links of the files of folder 1 and a copy of manifest.json. The Forge
folders were not changed. The probe ran the same check command in one heavy-run.

The probe gives 220 of 238 rows pass in folder 1, and 9 rows more than the real folder. Each of
the 9 rows now passes. Every remaining fail is a row with no job. The union would then be 224 of
229, and the 5 open rows would be the 5 expected rows. So the 9 rows hold good pictures. They
fail only on the version fields of the delivered manifest.

The writer of that manifest is not in this repo. The only code here that reads selectedVersion is
the checker and its test fixtures. The fix belongs to the Forge hand-off. No new Forge render is
needed for the 9 rows.

Because the values differ, edit.py was not run. The plan keeps the line `- [ ] Task 2.7: the
delivery check`.

